IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`
IMPORT `tas-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 41 to 45: connotation of phrases, titles, legislative references, administrative terms.
-- Every defined term of these sections has a row in tas-terms.l4; the rules here are for the definitions that have conditions, lists, dates or places in them.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- A definition worded "means" is a closed list, so a thing outside it is JUST FALSE; a definition worded "includes" is not closed, so a thing outside it is NOTHING.
-- ss 42, 43(3) and 45A are shown only as rows of dots and are not encoded.

§ `s 41: connotation of certain phrases`

-- src:837 | (1) In any Act the expressions person and party respectively shall include any body of persons, corporate or unincorporate, other than the Crown.
@ref s 41(1) (src:837)
GIVEN `the body is a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(1): the expressions person and party include the body` `the body is a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` `the body is the Crown` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the body is the Crown` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the body is a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:841 | committed for trial, used in any Act in relation to a person, shall mean committed to prison with the view of being tried as for a crime or admitted to bail and be so tried.
@ref s 41(2) (src:841)
GIVEN `the expression is used in an Act in relation to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is committed to prison with the view of being tried as for a crime` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is admitted to bail and is so tried` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(2): the person is committed for trial` `the expression is used in an Act in relation to a person` `the person is committed to prison with the view of being tried as for a crime` `the person is admitted to bail and is so tried` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the expression is used in an Act in relation to a person`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the person is committed to prison with the view of being tried as for a crime` OR `the person is admitted to bail and is so tried` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:843 | (3) The words oath and affidavit, used in any Act in relation to a person allowed by law to affirm in lieu of swearing, shall include affirmation and declaration, and the word swear in the like case shall include affirm and declare.
@ref s 41(3) (src:843)
GIVEN `the words are used in an Act in relation to a person allowed by law to affirm in lieu of swearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word used` IS A STRING
      `the other word` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(3): the word used includes the other word` `the words are used in an Act in relation to a person allowed by law to affirm in lieu of swearing` `the word used` `the other word` MEANS
    IF `the words are used in an Act in relation to a person allowed by law to affirm in lieu of swearing`
       AND (((`the word used` EQUALS "oath" OR `the word used` EQUALS "affidavit") AND (`the other word` EQUALS "affirmation" OR `the other word` EQUALS "declaration"))
            OR (`the word used` EQUALS "swear" AND (`the other word` EQUALS "affirm" OR `the other word` EQUALS "declare")))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 41(1): the expressions person and party include the body` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(1): the expressions person and party include the body` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(1): the expressions person and party include the body` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(2): the person is committed for trial` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(2): the person is committed for trial` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(2): the person is committed for trial` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(2): the person is committed for trial` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3): the word used includes the other word` TRUE "oath" "affirmation" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3): the word used includes the other word` TRUE "affidavit" "declaration" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3): the word used includes the other word` TRUE "swear" "affirm" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3): the word used includes the other word` TRUE "swear" "declare" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3): the word used includes the other word` TRUE "swear" "affirmation" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3): the word used includes the other word` TRUE "oath" "affirm" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3): the word used includes the other word` FALSE "oath" "affirmation" EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 43: meaning of certain titles and the like`

DECLARE `Territory of the Commonwealth` IS ONE OF
    `the Australian Capital Territory`
    `the Jervis Bay Territory`
    `the Northern Territory`
    `a Territory other than those three`

-- src:871 | internal Territory means the Australian Capital Territory, the Jervis Bay Territory or the Northern Territory;
@ref s 43(1) internal Territory (src:871)
GIVEN territory IS A `Territory of the Commonwealth`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(1): the Territory is an internal Territory` territory MEANS
    territory EQUALS `the Australian Capital Territory` OR territory EQUALS `the Jervis Bay Territory` OR territory EQUALS `the Northern Territory`

-- src:861 | external Territory means a Territory, other than an internal Territory, for the government of which as a Territory, provision is made by a Commonwealth Act;
@ref s 43(1) external Territory (src:861)
GIVEN territory IS A `Territory of the Commonwealth`
      `provision is made for its government as a Territory by a Commonwealth Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(1): the Territory is an external Territory` territory `provision is made for its government as a Territory by a Commonwealth Act` MEANS
    (NOT (`s 43(1): the Territory is an internal Territory` territory)) AND `provision is made for its government as a Territory by a Commonwealth Act`

-- src:853 | Australia means the Commonwealth of Australia and, when used in a geographical sense, does not include an external Territory;
@ref s 43(1) Australia (src:853)
GIVEN `the expression is used in a geographical sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is an external Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(1): Australia includes the place` `the expression is used in a geographical sense` `the place is an external Territory` MEANS
    IF `the expression is used in a geographical sense` AND `the place is an external Territory` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:863 | foreign country means any country, whether or not an independent sovereign State, outside Australia and the external Territories;
@ref s 43(1) foreign country (src:863)
GIVEN `it is a country, whether or not an independent sovereign State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is outside Australia and the external Territories` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(1): the place is a foreign country` `it is a country, whether or not an independent sovereign State` `it is outside Australia and the external Territories` MEANS
    `it is a country, whether or not an independent sovereign State` AND `it is outside Australia and the external Territories`

-- src:855 | British possession shall mean any part of the Sovereign's dominions, exclusive of the United Kingdom, and, where parts of such dominions are under both a central and a local legislature, all parts under such central legislature shall be deemed, for the purposes of this definition, to be one possession;
@ref s 43(1) British possession (src:855)
GIVEN `it is a part of the Sovereign's dominions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(1): the place is a British possession` `it is a part of the Sovereign's dominions` `it is the United Kingdom` MEANS
    `it is a part of the Sovereign's dominions` AND (NOT (`it is the United Kingdom`))

-- src:865 | Government Printer includes a person –
-- src:867 | (a) authorised by the Government of this State to print any matter; or
-- src:869 | (b) approved by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel under section 6(10) of the Legislation Publication Act 1996;
@ref s 43(1) Government Printer (src:865-869)
GIVEN `the person is authorised by the Government of this State to print any matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is approved by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel under section 6(10) of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(1): the Government Printer includes the person` `the person is authorised by the Government of this State to print any matter` `the person is approved by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel under section 6(10) of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` MEANS
    IF `the person is authorised by the Government of this State to print any matter` OR `the person is approved by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel under section 6(10) of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- The forty-second parallel of latitude is taken as 42 degrees south, the State lying wholly in the southern hemisphere.
-- A place on the parallel itself is in neither Division: the text says "to the north of" and "to the south of" (see NOTES.md).
DECLARE `Division of the State` IS ONE OF
    `the Northern Division`
    `the Southern Division`

-- src:875 | Northern Division, or words of similar import, used in relation to this State, shall be deemed to refer to all that part of the State situate or lying to the north of the forty-second parallel of latitude;
-- src:879 | Southern Division or words of similar import, used in relation to this State, shall be deemed to refer to all that part of the State situate or lying to the south of the forty-second parallel of latitude;
@ref s 43(1) Northern Division and Southern Division (src:875) (src:879)
GIVEN `degrees of south latitude of the place` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Division of the State`)
`s 43(1): the Division of the State in which the place lies` `degrees of south latitude of the place` MEANS
    IF `degrees of south latitude of the place` BELOW 42
    THEN JUST `the Northern Division`
    ELSE IF `degrees of south latitude of the place` GREATER THAN 42
         THEN JUST `the Southern Division`
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:887 | the Governor shall mean the Governor of this State, or the person for the time being administering the government of this State, acting with the advice of the Executive Council;
@ref s 43(1) the Governor (src:887)
GIVEN `the person is the Governor of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is for the time being administering the government of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with the advice of the Executive Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(1): the person is the Governor` `the person is the Governor of this State` `the person is for the time being administering the government of this State` `the person acts with the advice of the Executive Council` MEANS
    (`the person is the Governor of this State` OR `the person is for the time being administering the government of this State`) AND `the person acts with the advice of the Executive Council`

DECLARE `Way the State is referred to` IS ONE OF
    `the State`
    `this State`
    `Tasmania`
    `some other name`

-- src:891 | (1A) In any Act, a reference to the State, this State or Tasmania is a reference to the State of Tasmania and its dependencies.
@ref s 43(1A) (src:891)
GIVEN `the reference is in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      name IS A `Way the State is referred to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(1A): the reference is a reference to the State of Tasmania and its dependencies` `the reference is in an Act` name MEANS
    IF `the reference is in an Act` AND NOT (name EQUALS `some other name`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Region of the State` IS ONE OF
    `the northern area or region`
    `the north-western area or region`
    `the southern area or region`

`the councils of the northern area or region` MEANS LIST "Launceston", "Break O'Day", "Dorset", "Flinders", "George Town", "Meander Valley", "Northern Midlands", "West Tamar"

`the councils of the north-western area or region` MEANS LIST "Burnie", "Devonport", "Central Coast", "Circular Head", "Kentish", "King Island", "Latrobe", "Waratah-Wynyard", "West Coast"

`the councils of the southern area or region` MEANS LIST "Hobart", "Clarence", "Glenorchy", "Brighton", "Central Highlands", "Glamorgan-Spring Bay", "Huon Valley", "Kingborough", "New Norfolk", "Sorell", "Southern Midlands", "Tasman"

-- src:895 | northern area or northern region means that part of the State comprising the city of Launceston and the municipal areas of Break O'Day, Dorset, Flinders, George Town, Meander Valley, Northern Midlands and West Tamar;
-- src:897 | north-western area or north-western region means that part of the State comprising the cities of Burnie and Devonport and the municipal areas of Central Coast, Circular Head, Kentish, King Island, Latrobe, Waratah-Wynyard and West Coast;
-- src:899 | southern area or southern region means that part of the State comprising the cities of Hobart, Clarence and Glenorchy and the municipal areas of Brighton, Central Highlands, Glamorgan-Spring Bay, Huon Valley, Kingborough, New Norfolk, Sorell, Southern Midlands and Tasman.
@ref s 43(2) (src:895-899)
GIVEN council IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Region of the State`)
`s 43(2): the area or region comprising the city or municipal area` council MEANS
    BRANCH IF elem council `the councils of the northern area or region` THEN JUST `the northern area or region`
           IF elem council `the councils of the north-western area or region` THEN JUST `the north-western area or region`
           IF elem council `the councils of the southern area or region` THEN JUST `the southern area or region`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

