#ASSERT `s 43(1A): the reference is a reference to the State of Tasmania and its dependencies` TRUE `the State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 43(1A): the reference is a reference to the State of Tasmania and its dependencies` TRUE `this State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 43(1A): the reference is a reference to the State of Tasmania and its dependencies` TRUE `Tasmania` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 43(1A): the reference is a reference to the State of Tasmania and its dependencies` TRUE `some other name` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 43(1A): the reference is a reference to the State of Tasmania and its dependencies` FALSE `Tasmania` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 43(2): the area or region comprising the city or municipal area` "Launceston" EQUALS JUST `the northern area or region`
#ASSERT `s 43(2): the area or region comprising the city or municipal area` "West Tamar" EQUALS JUST `the northern area or region`
#ASSERT `s 43(2): the area or region comprising the city or municipal area` "Burnie" EQUALS JUST `the north-western area or region`
#ASSERT `s 43(2): the area or region comprising the city or municipal area` "Waratah-Wynyard" EQUALS JUST `the north-western area or region`
#ASSERT `s 43(2): the area or region comprising the city or municipal area` "Hobart" EQUALS JUST `the southern area or region`
#ASSERT `s 43(2): the area or region comprising the city or municipal area` "Tasman" EQUALS JUST `the southern area or region`
#ASSERT `s 43(2): the area or region comprising the city or municipal area` "Sydney" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT count `the councils of the northern area or region` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT count `the councils of the north-western area or region` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT count `the councils of the southern area or region` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN c YIELD (`s 43(2): the area or region comprising the city or municipal area` c) EQUALS JUST `the northern area or region`) (append `the councils of the northern area or region` (append `the councils of the north-western area or region` `the councils of the southern area or region`))) EQUALS 8

§ `s 44: legislative references`

DECLARE `Legislature` IS ONE OF
    `the Parliament of the Commonwealth`
    `the Parliament of the United Kingdom`
    `the Parliament of Tasmania`

-- src:907 | Australia Acts means –
-- src:909 | (a) the Australia Act 1986 of the Commonwealth; and
-- src:911 | (b) the Australia Act 1986 of the United Kingdom;
@ref s 44 Australia Acts (src:907-911)
GIVEN legislature IS A `Legislature`
      title IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44: the Act is one of the Australia Acts` legislature title MEANS
    title EQUALS "Australia Act 1986" AND (legislature EQUALS `the Parliament of the Commonwealth` OR legislature EQUALS `the Parliament of the United Kingdom`)

-- src:915 | Imperial Parliament shall mean the Parliament of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland or the Parliament of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland, according as it relates to a matter before or since 12th April 1927;
@ref s 44 Imperial Parliament (src:915)
GIVEN `the day of the matter` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 44: the Imperial Parliament, as it relates to a matter on the day, is the Parliament of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and` `the day of the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 44: a matter is before 12th April 1927` `the day of the matter`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST before THEN IF before THEN JUST "Ireland" ELSE JUST "Northern Ireland"

#ASSERT `s 44: the Act is one of the Australia Acts` `the Parliament of the Commonwealth` "Australia Act 1986"
#ASSERT `s 44: the Act is one of the Australia Acts` `the Parliament of the United Kingdom` "Australia Act 1986"
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44: the Act is one of the Australia Acts` `the Parliament of Tasmania` "Australia Act 1986")
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44: the Act is one of the Australia Acts` `the Parliament of the Commonwealth` "Australia Act 1990")
#ASSERT `s 44: the Imperial Parliament, as it relates to a matter on the day, is the Parliament of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and` (Date 11 4 1927) EQUALS JUST "Ireland"
#ASSERT `s 44: the Imperial Parliament, as it relates to a matter on the day, is the Parliament of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and` (Date 13 4 1927) EQUALS JUST "Northern Ireland"
#ASSERT `s 44: the Imperial Parliament, as it relates to a matter on the day, is the Parliament of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and` (Date 12 4 1927) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 45: administrative terms`

-- src:925 | Appropriation Act means an Act which authorizes the issue and application of any money from the Public Account to meet –
-- src:927 | (a) the cost of the ordinary annual services of the Government; or
-- src:929 | (b) expenditure on public works or any property required for public purposes; or
-- src:931 | (c) the making of a loan authorized by law;
@ref s 45(1) Appropriation Act (src:925-931)
GIVEN `the Act authorizes the issue and application of money from the Public Account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to meet the cost of the ordinary annual services of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to meet expenditure on public works or any property required for public purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to meet the making of a loan authorized by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(1): the Act is an Appropriation Act` `the Act authorizes the issue and application of money from the Public Account` `to meet the cost of the ordinary annual services of the Government` `to meet expenditure on public works or any property required for public purposes` `to meet the making of a loan authorized by law` MEANS
    `the Act authorizes the issue and application of money from the Public Account` AND (`to meet the cost of the ordinary annual services of the Government` OR `to meet expenditure on public works or any property required for public purposes` OR `to meet the making of a loan authorized by law`)

-- src:945 | the Minister shall mean the Minister of the Crown for the time being administering the enactment in which, or in respect of which, the expression is used;
@ref s 45(1) the Minister (src:945)
GIVEN `the person is a Minister of the Crown for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is administering the enactment in which, or in respect of which, the expression is used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(1): the person is the Minister` `the person is a Minister of the Crown for the time being` `the person is administering the enactment in which, or in respect of which, the expression is used` MEANS
    `the person is a Minister of the Crown for the time being` AND `the person is administering the enactment in which, or in respect of which, the expression is used`

-- src:947 | order-in-council shall mean an order made by the Governor in Council;
@ref s 45(1) order-in-council (src:947)
GIVEN `the order is made by the Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(1): the order is an order-in-council` `the order is made by the Governor in Council` MEANS
    `the order is made by the Governor in Council`

-- src:951 | proclamation shall mean a proclamation made by the Governor and published or notified in the Gazette;
@ref s 45(1) proclamation (src:951)
GIVEN `the proclamation is made by the Governor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published or notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(1): the instrument is a proclamation` `the proclamation is made by the Governor` `it is published or notified in the Gazette` MEANS
    `the proclamation is made by the Governor` AND `it is published or notified in the Gazette`

-- src:957 | (2) Where –
-- src:959 | (a) the administration of an enactment (in this subsection referred to as "the relevant enactment") is assigned, in different respects, to separate Ministers; and
-- src:961 | (b) reference is made –
-- src:963 | (i) in the relevant enactment to the Minister or to the Department; or
-- src:965 | (ii) in another enactment to the Minister administering the relevant enactment or to the responsible Department in relation to the relevant enactment; and
-- src:967 | (c) that reference relates to the respects in which the administration of the relevant enactment is assigned to a particular Minister –
-- src:969 | that reference shall be interpreted accordingly.
@ref s 45(2) (src:957-969)
GIVEN `the administration of the relevant enactment is assigned, in different respects, to separate Ministers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reference is made in the relevant enactment to the Minister or the Department, or in another enactment to the Minister administering it or the responsible Department` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference relates to the respects in which the administration is assigned to a particular Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister to whom those respects are assigned` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 45(2): the reference is interpreted as a reference to` `the administration of the relevant enactment is assigned, in different respects, to separate Ministers` `reference is made in the relevant enactment to the Minister or the Department, or in another enactment to the Minister administering it or the responsible Department` `the reference relates to the respects in which the administration is assigned to a particular Minister` `the Minister to whom those respects are assigned` MEANS
    IF `the administration of the relevant enactment is assigned, in different respects, to separate Ministers`
       AND `reference is made in the relevant enactment to the Minister or the Department, or in another enactment to the Minister administering it or the responsible Department`
       AND `the reference relates to the respects in which the administration is assigned to a particular Minister`
    THEN JUST `the Minister to whom those respects are assigned`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:973 | assigned means assigned by order under section 4 of the Administrative Arrangements Act 1990;
@ref s 45(3) assigned (src:973)
GIVEN `it is assigned by order under section 4 of the Administrative Arrangements Act 1990` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(3): the administration is assigned` `it is assigned by order under section 4 of the Administrative Arrangements Act 1990` MEANS
    `it is assigned by order under section 4 of the Administrative Arrangements Act 1990`

-- src:977 | enactment means –
-- src:979 | (a) an Act; or
-- src:981 | (b) any other instrument of a legislative character; or
-- src:983 | (c) any provision or part of an Act or of an instrument referred to in paragraph (b).
@ref s 45(3) enactment (src:977-983)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `the instrument is of a legislative character` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a provision or part of an Act or of such an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(3): the thing is an enactment` kind `the instrument is of a legislative character` `the thing is a provision or part of an Act or of such an instrument` MEANS
    kind EQUALS `an Act` OR `the instrument is of a legislative character` OR `the thing is a provision or part of an Act or of such an instrument`

